-- title:
--   Absolutely unramified complete DVR with residue field 𝔽ᵣ is ℤᵣ
-- statement:
--   Let $r$ be a prime number and let $\mathcal{O}$ be a commutative ring which is a domain of characteristic zero, assumed to be a discrete valuation ring, with an irreducible element $\pi$ such that $\mathcal{O}$ is adically complete for the ideal $(\pi)$, the quotient $\mathcal{O}/(\pi)$ has cardinality exactly $r$ (as a natural number via `Nat.card`), and $\mathcal{O}$ is absolutely unramified in the sense that the ideal generated by the image of $r$ in $\mathcal{O}$ equals $(\pi)$. Let $K_0$ be a field of characteristic zero equipped with an $\mathcal{O}$-algebra structure making it a fraction field of $\mathcal{O}$. The conclusion asserts the existence of a ring isomorphism $e_{\mathcal{O}} : \mathbb{Z}_r \to \mathcal{O}$ and a ring isomorphism $e_K : \mathbb{Q}_r \to K_0$ which are compatible with the two inclusions of a ring into its fraction field: for every $x \in \mathbb{Z}_r$, the image of $e_{\mathcal{O}}(x)$ under the structure map $\mathcal{O} \to K_0$ equals $e_K$ applied to the image of $x$ in $\mathbb{Q}_r$.
--
--   This is the classical uniqueness statement for absolutely unramified complete discrete valuation rings of mixed characteristic with finite prime residue field: such a ring is the ring of Witt vectors $W(\mathbb{F}_r) = \mathbb{Z}_r$, compatibly with fraction fields. It is used in the Čerednik–Drinfeld part of the development, where local rings of integers arising there are identified with $\mathbb{Z}_r$ so that $p$-adic constructions (formal modules, moduli data, ramification of extensions) may be carried out over $\mathbb{Z}_r$ itself.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_CerednikDrinfeld_exists_ringEquiv_padicInt_algebraMap_apply_eq_of_isAdicComplete_of_natCard_quotient_eq.lean

